    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_112596a9451de5fe20f3f8f23bb94017522c43dac5ff163ac0e438828ea6aa72",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the source matches chaotic periodic orbits with primes, periods with log p, and their exponential counting laws, then notes that the oscillatory signs in the Riemann and dynamical trace formulas are opposite and reports Connes' absorption-spectrum interpretation. Interpretation: the dictionary preserves counting and repetition structure but fails to preserve sign; that obstruction changes the type of operator model suggested, shifting complexity to the function space rather than establishing an ordinary self-adjoint spectrum. Boundary: absorption is explicitly an interpretation, no Riemann Hamiltonian is constructed, and matched growth laws do not imply spectral equivalence or RH.",
