    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9c118946f38dd28e3819f03037fd0e70fc25a43d5d225096af2c818a7bf906ba",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Arithmeticity constrains traces across field embeddings, so the number of available trace values grows like the square root of the total orbit count; via the trace-length map this creates exponentially large exact length families. Their coherent multiplicity gain, inserted into the diagonal form factor, can reach order one near the Ehrenfest scale even though the underlying hyperbolic motion remains classically chaotic. The critical exponent is one half: non-arithmetic controls with subcritical exponential multiplicity need not depart from GOE. Hecke correspondences provide a separate commuting-operator picture of the same arithmetic exceptionalism, but the source does not derive Poisson statistics from that symmetry algebra.",
